    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d589">

                <pb facs="0499" n="383" xml:id="pg383"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/847.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Smith to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 17, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Department’s February 13. Because of doubt as to the effectiveness of the
                    Cape Haitien blockade and the question of whether recognition of the blockade
                    would not be a partial recognition of the Zamor Government and of Theodore as a
                    belligerent, the entire matter is held in abeyance.* * * Foreign representatives
                    continue to act in complete accord with the Legation, awaiting our action as to
                    recognition.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
